WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.560
<i>The distant future, 5012.</i>

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.320
<i>The glorious history of mankind
suddenly came to an end.</i>

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.110
<i>There was an invasion of Aliens
who flew in from outer space.</i>

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:21.750
<i>Human civilization was annihilated by
<Machine Lifeforms>, weapons deployed by the Aliens.</i>

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:27.540
<i>The miniscule population that survived
ended up fleeing to the moon.</i>

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.630
<i>The year 5204.</i>

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:35.010
<i>With a series of bases laid out
upon the orbital trajectory,</i>

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:38.850
<i>a rebellion operation began using androids.</i>

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.520
<i>Over a dozen large-scale
descent operations later,</i>

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.940
<i>we still have not been able
to deliver a decisive blow.</i>

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:52.030
<i>In order to break through the battlefront
which has entered a stalemate,</i>

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:55.650
<i>you YoRHa Soldiers exist.</i>

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.790
<i>Fulfill your duties
as the ultimate combat weapons.</i>

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.290
Yes. We understand.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.620
<i>I wish you luck.</i>

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.340
Glory to mankind!

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:11.960
Glory to mankind!

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.670
Glory... to mankind.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.260
Glory...

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:55.940
<i>A long time ago, a volcano erupted.</i>

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.820
<i>From the fires of the eruption,
God appeared.</i>

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:06.620
<i>This is what God said to the machines.</i>

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:13.830
<i>Conscience, pain, joy, sorrow,</i>

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:21.430
<i>anger, shame, solitude, future...</i>

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.760
<i>The meaning of life.</i>

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:44.240
CITY RUINS

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:37.710
AH...

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.210
AH... AAH..........

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.460
<i>Its guise was visible.</i>

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.880
<i>Its shape was visible.</i>

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:48.920
<i>However, its soul was not visible.</i>

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:54.390
<i>For the absence of an end from being able to see,
the machines learned hesitation.</i>

00:06:55.430 --> 00:07:01.600
<i>But at the same time,
the joy of learning fulfilled the machines.</i>

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:14.160
M... NAM... IS PLA...O...8. I...M A GENERAL FAI...E.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.310
There's still more!?

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:46.020
Damn it! I'm already out of bullets.

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.820
What’s it doing?

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.200
It's not attacking me?

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.830
<i>B-Big Brother.</i>

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.080
<i>Big Brother... Big Brother...</i>

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:04.290
<i>Big Brother... Big Brother...</i>

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.920
<i>Big Brother... Big Brother...</i>

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:11.380
<i>Big Brother... Big Brother...</i>

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:27.820
I FOUND IT ON THE BATTLEFIELD. A SMALL ITEM
CALLED A FLOWER DRAWN ON THAT PIECE OF PAPER

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:23.260
How was it?

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.850
Most of them have been taken
since last time.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.390
I believe this will be the last time.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.940
This place, too, huh?

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:31.310
Hey!

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:34.780
Load up all the resources from here!
Hurry!

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:39.570
The tin men nearby have been docile lately,
but we don't know what's going to happen.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:45.490
Hey. Can we really win this?

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:48.040
Oh, we'll make something of it!

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:52.380
I've heard that a new type of androids
called YoRHa have been deployed.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:55.090
Maybe it’ll be over really soon?

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.670
I sure hope so.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:06.560
<i>A declaration to androids struggling on Earth,
from the Council of Humanity on the moon.</i>

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:11.690
<i>Currently the battles against
machine lifeforms are at a stalemate.</i>

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:16.730
<i>You all must be exhausted
from an extended duration of combat.</i>

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:20.200
<i>However, I would like you
to continue striving without giving up.</i>

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:24.410
<i>For the several hundred thousand humans
on the surface of the Moon, winning Earth—</i>

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:30.710
Huh? You're not going to listen
to the end, Lily?

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:34.130
I know what they want to say.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.380
Basically they want us to fight
until we die, right?

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:42.890
Come on,
you always sound really harsh, Lily.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.430
Help me out here!

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.390
Jeez, she can't do it by herself?

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.600
Go help her.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:50.850
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.150
You need to stop that already.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:55.190
Roger that, Leader!

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:04.160
<i>The guys up on the moon
speak in high spirits.</i>

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:08.040
<i>But not even a single gun
has been given to us, the Resistance,</i>

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:10.000
<i>who've been fighting on ground
for centuries.</i>

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:16.210
<i>Including the fact that recent machine lifeforms
have been evolving,</i>

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:18.090
<i>the end is still not in sight.</i>

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:22.170
<i>Just how long will we...</i>

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:41.030
<i>B-Big Brother.</i>

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.420
Miss 2B, can you hear me?

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.420
I'm finished with the boot sequence.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.880
Good morning.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:03.260
Do you have any issues?

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:05.800
I'm fine.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:07.720
9S.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:08.640
Yes?

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:12.890
Your voice. It somehow puts me at ease.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.400
Th-Thank you so much!

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:22.320
As the one in charge of your maintenance,
that makes me really happy.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:25.570
Actually, me too. When I hear your voice—

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:26.360
9S.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:27.950
Y-Yes?

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:31.330
The Commander is calling.
I'll go on ahead.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.540
Huh?

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:45.550
Commander.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:48.640
Oh, 2B and 9S.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.470
Are you done with the maintenance?

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:51.470
Yes.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:54.980
You detonated your black box
in order to defeat the enemy.

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:56.480
Don't be too reckless, okay?

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:57.900
Okay.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:02.570
I hate to say this right after your maintenance,
but I have a mission for you.

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:06.900
Rendezvous with the Resistance on the surface,
and do some recon.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:13.620
Wasn't a different YoRHa member assigned
as liaison with the Resistance?

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:16.910
We haven't been able to contact them
for a while now.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:21.380
I'd like you to do some onsite investigation,
including the reason for the lack of comms.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:24.420
Concentrate your search
in the desert area.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.300
Understood.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:34.470
But why would a combat model like Miss 2B
be assigned for a reconnaissance?

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:38.480
We Scanner models
are enough for onsite recon.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.560
Don't complain about your orders.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:41.770
Okay.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:45.230
2B... 9S...

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.150
Be careful.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:53.240
As soon as we're done loading,
we'll head to the next resource storage!

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:56.120
Go on ahead and scout
as soon as you're able to!

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:59.160
Don't be workin' so slow, you twins!

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:01.250
Hurry and clean that up, so we can...

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:05.340
Enemy attack!

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:08.260
Damn it! Don't let it get close!

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:16.310
Retreat! Retreat! Abandon the resources!

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:19.440
Load the wounded
onto the remaining trucks! Hurry!

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:30.150
<i>B-Big Brother.</i>

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.000
<i>The machine found them.</i>

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:52.090
<i>The machine called them "treasures."</i>

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:57.180
<i>Each treasure had a different shape.</i>

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:00.100
<i>Each treasure had...</i>

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:03.100
<i>a different shape.</i>

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:10.320
<i>Kill... Kill... Kill...</i>

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:16.160
<i>Kill... Kill... Kill...</i>

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.620
The minefield is useless.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:22.710
How are the injured?

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.710
What about the distress call to the camp?

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:27.670
We won't last until they arrive!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:30.210
Wh-What about an assistance request
to the Council of Humanity?

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:34.130
How many times do I have to tell you?
Those guys will never send any assistance!

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:40.890
We'll lure them out to the valley up ahead,
and then drop the bridge!

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:43.230
If you’re alive, follow me!

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:49.650
Here they come.

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:51.570
What is it?

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.200
There’s one strange one.

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:56.320
Don't mind it.
Draw them in really close, then drop them.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.540
They've passed the center!

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:05.880
Now!

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:07.750
What's wrong?

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:09.550
No way. Did it break?

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:11.590
What are you doing? Set it off already!

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.880
Damn it. It won't explode!

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.550
If only Jackass was here right now!

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:20.140
Leader! It's useless! Let's retreat!

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:25.100
Leader!

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.910
Who in the world...

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:32.130
<i>K-Kill—</i>

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:40.890
N-Number Two.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:43.890
There.

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:47.140
Miss 2B, we have completed
the suppression now.

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:47.980
Yeah.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:51.690
I'll return the flight units
back to the Bunker via autopilot.

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:56.400
Well, machine lifeforms
often act in groups,

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:59.240
but this time
it was on quite a large scale.

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.820
<i>Alert. Enemy signals detected.</i>

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:03.830
Miss 2B, there are still survivors!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.000
<i>Kill...</i>

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:11.080
Pod!

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:24.100
Okay, everyone. It’s all right now.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:25.890
Stop!

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:28.680
Lily!

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:33.940
Pod, give me some staunching gel
and the logic-virus vaccine.

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.480
Don't worry about me! Hey!

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:42.200
They are...

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:45.370
They're maintenance units
permanently stationed with the Resistance.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:50.210
But anyway! Those black outfits and blindfolds.
You guys must be YoRHa Soldiers!

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:53.210
This is the first time
I've actually met YoRHa Soldiers!

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:57.090
The Council of Humanity
answered our requests!

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:59.380
- Yeah!
- Right, Lily?

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:01.630
I had my faith in the Council of Humanity.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.840
You were scared and gave up earlier.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:05.470
You were scared too!

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.640
- I wasn't scared!
- You definitely were!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.640
We'll head back to camp for now.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:09.140
I can't hear you!

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:10.060
You two, we'll talk once we get there.

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:13.730
<i>For the Council of Humanity
to send reinforcements...</i>

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.860
<i>Killed Father.</i>

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:22.360
<i>Killed Mother.</i>

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:26.120
<i>Killed Father.</i>

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:29.080
<i>Killed Mother.</i>

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:33.620
<i>Coldly grasped in those hands
was the joy of growth,</i>

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:39.960
<i>and the solitude of becoming alone.</i>

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:52.230
<i>At this rate... At this rate...
At this rate... At this rate...</i>

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:59.230
<i>At this rate... At this rate...
At this rate... At this rate...</i>

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:03.490
<i>At this rate... I-It's no good!</i>

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:43.000
POD 042 REPORTING TO ALL OF MANKIND.

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:43.000
WE WILL NOW EXECUTE THE TASK
OF INTRODUCING THE MULTIPLE ENDINGS
FOR THE VIDEO GAME "NIER:AUTOMATA." OVER.

00:22:44.380 --> 00:22:47.260
PUPPET PLAY
NIER:AUTOMATA
“HANDLE WITH CARE”

00:22:50.140 --> 00:22:51.470
Yes, yes! Hello!

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:56.270
We are androids who fight for mankind
day in and day out, YoRHa No. 9 Type S AKA 9S and...

00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:59.190
Likewise, YoRHa No. 2 Type B AKA 2B.

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:01.270
Today, we have a postcard with a question

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:05.570
from one of the good kids
watching this on TV, Taro Yoko from Aichi.

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:08.150
TO: NIER:AUTOMATA
QUESTION SEGMENT
FROM: TARO YOKO IN AICHI

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:08.150
*CURRENTLY, SENDING IN QUESTIONS FOR THIS SEGMENT
HAS COME TO AND END

00:23:05.570 --> 00:23:07.110
That name sounds familiar.

00:23:08.450 --> 00:23:12.830
I have two questions.
First, what is the androids' energy source?

00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:13.240
Q. WHAT IS THE ANDROIDS' "ENERGY" SOURCE?

00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:15.740
Answer to the first question.
Our energy comes from... water.

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:20.210
That's right! Ordinary androids
drink purified water through their mouths,

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:17.960
ORDINARY ANDROIDS

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:19.920
ORDINARY ANDROIDS
DRINK PURIFIED WATER THROUGH MOUTH

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:21.500
YoRHa MODELS

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:22.750
but YoRHa model androids
automatically replenish

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:24.550
YoRHa MODELS
AUTOMATICALLY REPLENISH THE REACTORS

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:25.340
their reactors from internal tanks
through chambers!

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:29.090
Q. WHAT IS THE "OS CHIP"
THAT IS INSTALLED ON AN ANDROID?

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:29.970
Second question, what is the OS chip
that is equipped on an android?

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:31.840
Wait, I have a bad feeling about this.

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:32.600
REMOVE OS CHIP?
[YES] [NO]

00:23:32.140 --> 00:23:33.600
Miss 2B, wa—

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:37.680
Caution. Handle With Care!
Removal of the OS chip will result in death.

00:23:38.390 --> 00:23:40.020
TO BE CONTINUED
